new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3210d81
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/hdmi5-test-build.md
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+# Frame Pro HDMI 5 test build
+
+This build adds an opt-in PlayStation 5 / HDMI 5 tile for the owner's
+QE65LS03FWUXXU (Tizen 9). It keeps app ID `DclHome001.Home`, package
+`DclHome001`, and the existing service identity. It does not change native Home,
+startup, signing profiles, or certificates.
+
+## Evidence and implementation
+
+On this TV, `VIDEOSOURCE` exposes only one provider containing HDMI 1–4.
+When Samsung Home selects the panel's HDMI 5 socket, `tvwindow.getSource()`
+throws `UnknownError: Unknown source type`. However, authenticated local IP
+Control on HTTPS port 1516 reports `getTVStates.inputSource = HDMI5`, and the
+owner confirmed `inputSourceControl` with `inputSource: HDMI5` switches from
+Tanix / HDMI 4 to PS5.
+
+The background service owns HTTPS and reads/writes a package-private 0600 token
+file. Its certificate exception applies only to the configured local TV's
+self-signed IP Control endpoint. Tokens are not placed in the widget, browser,
+preferences, logs, or status responses. The service binds its control endpoint
+only to loopback. Token setup travels over the authenticated Developer Mode
+SDB connection and requires the native control header with no browser Origin.
+The UI receives only configuration status and current input. Only the fixed
+`getTVStates` and `inputSourceControl(HDMI5)` methods are available.
+
+The opt-in tile uses IP Control and then opens `org.tizen.tv-viewer`. It never
+passes a synthetic source to TVWindow. Existing native HDMI inputs remain on
+their existing path. The input state is refreshed when the launcher resumes;
+there is no new polling loop or automatic command retry.
+
+## Install the supplied compiled widget
+
+Extract `AeroTizen-HDMI5-test.zip` into Downloads. Stop `inspect launcher`
+with Ctrl+C first so its connection is released. In the folder containing your
+existing AeroTizen CLI, run:
+
+```sh
+./aerotizen --tv 192.168.1.50 install "$HOME/Downloads/AeroTizen-HDMI5-test/AeroTizen-HDMI5-unsigned.wgt"
+```
+
+This uses the CLI's existing certificate profile to update in place. Do not
+uninstall the existing app or regenerate certificates. If the CLI says no
+certificates exist, stop and inspect the profile location rather than creating
+a new app identity.
+
+Open AeroTizen on the TV and let its Home screen load. Then transfer the
+existing token (it remains on the Mac as well):
+
+```sh
+python3 "$HOME/Downloads/AeroTizen-HDMI5-test/tools/configure-hdmi5.py" --tv 192.168.1.50
+python3 "$HOME/Downloads/AeroTizen-HDMI5-test/tools/configure-hdmi5.py" --tv 192.168.1.50 --check
+```
+
+The default token file is
+`~/.config/cleanframe-hdmi-diagnostics/ip-control-token.json`, created by the
+owner's successful IP Control test. Do not paste its contents into chat.
+Return to AeroTizen Home to refresh Inputs; the PS5 tile should appear.
+Select it once from another input and confirm the PS5 picture appears.
+Use the physical Home button to return.
+
+If a different token path is needed, pass `--token-file /path/to/file.json`.
+If the TV's address changes, provision again using its new `--tv` address.
+There is no pairing or token renewal in the setup tool.
+
+To remove this opt-in without changing Home or other preferences:
+
+```sh
+python3 "$HOME/Downloads/AeroTizen-HDMI5-test/tools/configure-hdmi5.py" --tv 192.168.1.50 --disable
+```
+
+Return to AeroTizen Home to refresh Inputs. Your original token on the Mac
+is retained. A standard AeroTizen widget can later replace the test build
+through the same CLI install command, without uninstalling.
+
+## Validation and limits
+
+Build, type checks, formatting, lint, 306 Node tests, and the compiled-browser
+HDMI 5 test passed. The browser test covers a TV API that omits HDMI 5 and
+throws on active-source reads, tile visibility with disconnected inputs hidden,
+one POST per activation, native viewer handoff, and no synthetic TVWindow calls.
+Service tests cover private persistence, token redaction, origin restrictions,
+fixed commands, overlapping calls, failure without retries, and disable.
+
+The owner has validated Mac-to-TV IP Control switching. Background-service-to-TV
+HTTPS, the transferred token's acceptance from the TV itself, and native viewer
+handoff on this physical firmware still require the installation test.
+
+Upstream base: `94b4df2e27b158d1ac08cf2f5f9a73ddcc4e2646` (launcher 2.7.0).
+The archive includes the complete source diff, setup client, and upstream license.
